.²1 A sacred precept or rule, law, ordinance.
.²2 A prescribed rule, a prescribed alternative, optional rule; {#praBuH#}
 {#praTamakalpasya yo'nukalpena vartate#} <ls>Ms. 11. 30</ls> ‘able to follow the
 prescribed rule to be observed in preference to all others’; {#praTamaH#}
 {#kalpaH#} <ls>M. 1</ls>; <ab>cf.</ab> also <ls>Pratimā 4</ls>, and <ls>Abhiṣeka. 6</ls> and <ls>Ś. 4</ls>.
 a very good (or best) alternative; {#eza vE praTamaH kalpaH pradAne havyakavyayoH#} <ls>Ms. 3. 147</ls>.
.²3 (Hence) A proposal, suggestion, resolve, determination; {#eza me praTamaH#}
 {#kalpaH#} <ls>Rām. 2. 52. 63</ls>; {#udAraH kalpaH#} <ls>Ś. 7</ls>.
.²4 Manner of acting, procedure, form, way, method (in religious rites);
 {#SrUyate hi purAkalpe#} <ls>Mb. 6. 43. 23</ls>; {#kzAtreRa kalpenopanIya#} <ls>U. 2</ls>;
 {#kalpavitkalpayAmAsa vanyAmevAsya saMviDAm#} <ls>R. 1. 94</ls>; <ls>Ms. 7. 185</ls>.
.²5 End of the world, universal destruction.
.²6 A day of Brahmā or 1,000 Yugas, being a period of 432 million years
 of mortals and measuring the duration of the world; <ab>cf.</ab> <ls>Bhāg. 3. 11</ls>;
 {#SrISvetavArAhakalpe#} [the

 one in which we now live]; {#kalpaM sTitaM tanuBftAM tanuBistataH kim#}
 <ls>Śānti. 4. 2</ls>. Hence {#kAlpika#} means ‘born in the primeval age’ <ls>Bu. Ch. 2. 48</ls>.
.²7 Medical treatment of the sick.
.²8 One of the six Vedāṅgas, {%<ab>i. e.</ab>%} that which lays down the ritual
 and prescribes rules for ceremonial and sacrificial acts; {#SikzA kalpo#}
 {#vyAkaraRam#} <ls>Muṇḍ. 1. 1. 5</ls> see under {#vedANga#}.
.²9 A termination added to nouns and adjectives in the sense of ‘a little
 less than’, ‘almost like’, ‘nearly equal to’, <ls>P. V. 3. 67</ls> [denoting similarity
 with a degree of inferiority]; {#kumArakalpaM suzuve kumAram#} <ls>R. 5. 36</ls>;
 {#upapannametadasminnfzikalpe rAjani#} <ls>Ś. 2</ls>; {#praBAtakalpA SaSineva#}
 {#SarvarI#} <ls>R. 3. 2</ls>; so {#mftakalpaH, pratipannakalpaH#} <ab>&c.</ab>
.²10 The doctrine of poisons and antidotes.
.²11 One of the trees of paradise; <ab>cf.</ab> {#kalpadruma#}.
.²12 Vigour, strength; {#lOkike samayAcAre kftakalpo viSAradaH#} <ls>Rām. 2. 1. 22</ls>.

